.TH SDL_HINT_CPU_FEATURE_MASK 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_CPU_FEATURE_MASK \- A variable that limits what CPU features are available.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_CPU_FEATURE_MASK \(dqSDL_CPU_FEATURE_MASK\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default, SDL marks all features the current CPU supports as available\[char46] This hint allows the enabled features to be limited to a subset\[char46]
.PP
When the hint is unset, or empty, SDL will enable all detected CPU features\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to a comma separated list containing the following items:
.PP

\(bu \(dqall\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqaltivec\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqsse\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqsse2\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqsse3\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqsse41\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqsse42\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqavx\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqavx2\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqavx512f\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqarm-simd\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqneon\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqsve2\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqlsx\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqlasx\(dq
.PP
The items can be prefixed by \(aq+\(aq/\(aq-\(aq to add/remove features\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

